  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/IqcmEXqvu0_gtK-Jaqdd_YoJRXM4WUG9XOwGe_d2JDI.original.fullsize.png\"><br />By Gauss law $\\int \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}} \\cdot \\mathrm{d} \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{A}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_{\\mathrm{in}}}{\\varepsilon_0}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{EdA}=\\frac{\\sigma \\times \\mathrm{dA}}{\\varepsilon_0} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\sigma}{\\varepsilon_0}\n\\end{aligned}$",
